	(footprint "EnOcean:TCM515_HandSolder"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "1a3c1814-9eca-4717-a16a-8d416222c42a")
		(at 127.6 114 -90)
		(descr "EnOcean TCM 515 / 515U / 515J, 31 castellated pads, 19 x 14.7 mm. Pad geometry from TCM 515 User Manual v1.22 (Jan 2024), Figure 15: 1.0 mm pitch, pad centres 0.6 mm inside the outline, pad 0.7 x 1.5, solder resist 0.8 x 1.6, stencil 0.6 x 1.4. Hand-solder variant: every pad 0.5 mm longer to the outside (2.0 mm, 0.65 mm past the module edge), so the iron reaches the castellation; inner pad ends unchanged. Courtyard stays around the module body: the extensions are bare copper. Keep top copper out from under the module (live test points on its underside, chapter 11.5); keep metal out of the half-disc next to pin 2.")
